{"Accessing integration.metadata[\"sender\"][\"login\"] without guarding against missing keys will raise a KeyError if the webhook event didn't include a sender field": 0.9448999166488647, "The redirect_uri and state parameters are appended to the URL without URL-encoding, which could cause issues if they contain special characters like &, =, or +, resulting in malformed or misinterpreted redirect URLs": 0.8661947846412659, "The bare except Exception silently swallows all errors (network failures, unexpected response formats, etc.) without logging, making failures unobservable in production": 0.883365273475647, "The OAuth access token obtained is used only to look up the GitHub username and then discarded without being revoked, leaving a valid user token persisting on GitHub's side": 0.5957936644554138, "The function name error is very generic and shadows any module-level error name that might be imported in the future": 0.11794914305210114, "The installation_id is bound to pipeline state only when present in the initial GET request; if the user navigates directly to the setup URL with a state param but without installation_id, the code will proceed without an installation_id ever being stored": 0.4818636178970337, "The hardcoded state value in test_github_user_mismatch lacks a comment explaining where this value comes from, making it unclear why the state check passes": 0.042341139167547226, "safe_urlopen (line 423) is outside the try/except block, so network errors, timeouts, or RestrictedIPAddress exceptions will propagate as unhandled 500 errors": 0.9787946939468384, "get_user_info (line 434) calls resp.raise_for_status() internally, which raises requests.exceptions.HTTPError on 4xx/5xx responses from GitHub's /user endpoint, also unhandled": 0.9595831632614136}